terminal/

# Tool-written files under a managed directory. Unlike everything above, this is
# not a source-dir entry: patterns match the *target* path, and this one names a
# file in $HOME that must never become managed. lazy.nvim rewrites
# ~/.config/nvim/lazy-lock.json on every :Lazy update, so tracking it would put
# `chezmoi status` permanently out of sync.
#
# Belt-and-braces, not the mechanism: what actually keeps it untracked is that it
# is never added to the source dir. chezmoi documents .chezmoiignore as matching
# target paths but does not say whether `chezmoi add` honours it, so this entry's
# only guaranteed effect is to stop an accidentally-added lockfile from being
# applied over yours.
.config/nvim/lazy-lock.json
